---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About wReady — a personal creative workbench.">
	<main class="about">
		<h1>About wReady</h1>

		<p>
			wReady is a personal creative workbench for storing, writing, and managing creative work
			across screenplays, songs, poems, short stories, and blog posts. All content lives as
			MDX files in version-controlled content collections, validated with Zod schemas, and
			rendered through Astro.
		</p>

		<h2>Architecture</h2>
		<p>
			Built on Astro 6 with a static-first philosophy. The site ships zero client-side JavaScript
			by default. Alpine.js handles the few interactive features (chord analyser, scene filters,
			tension graphs). A custom remark plugin parses screenplay shorthand into formatted components
			at build time.
		</p>

		<h2>Current Project</h2>
		<p>
			The primary creative project is <em>Her Majesty's Displeasure</em> &mdash; a six-part limited
			series screenplay. A dark political satire set in the late 1960s, following a fictional MI5
			operation to surveil John Lennon after The Beatles receive their MBEs.
		</p>

		<h2>Stack</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Astro 6 &mdash; static-first framework with server endpoints</li>
			<li>MDX + Content Collections &mdash; structured content with Zod-validated frontmatter</li>
			<li>Alpine.js &mdash; lightweight client-side interactivity</li>
			<li>Vanilla CSS &mdash; dark, editorial aesthetic with custom properties</li>
			<li>Netlify &mdash; deployment adapter</li>
		</ul>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.about h1 {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.about h2 {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.about ul {
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
	}

	.about li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
